(F5 T2 V4c: element_beam_force_moment (manual Professional 6.416), the
 manual example: a beam with a constant z moment of 10 gives
 element_beam_force_moment 0 0 0 0 0 -10 0 0 0 0 0 10 (first node with
 the minus). 3D cantilever along x WITHOUT a local z record (the classic
 GNU beam in the x-y plane, the Professional default local z = global z
 for this beam), tip moment 10 about z, tip velx fixed. E 1, Izz 4.
 Expected, =
 Professional 02-08-2026: element_beam_force_moment 1 = 0 0 0 0 0 -10 0
 0 0 0 0 10; node_dof 2 vely 1.25 rotz 2.5.
 group_beam_memory -total_linear (the Professional default beam memory;
 the GNU default -updated rotates the beam chord: BEAM-MEMORY-DEFAULT).)
echo -no
number_of_space_dimensions 3
materi_velocity
materi_displacement
beam_rotation
end_initia
node 1 0 0 0
node 2 1 0 0
element 1 -beam 1 2
group_type 0 -beam
group_beam_young 0 1
group_beam_shear 0 1
group_beam_inertia 0 1 4 1
group_beam_memory 0 -total_linear
bounda_dof 0 1 -velx -vely -velz -rotx -roty -rotz
bounda_dof 2 2 -velx
bounda_force 1 2 -rotz
bounda_time 1 10.
control_timestep 0 1. 1.
end_data
